.Dd January 25, 2026
.Dt DRIVER 9
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm struct driver
.Nd generic device driver interface
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In kern/driver.h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Vt struct driver
structure represents a loadable device driver in the kernel. It defines the interface between the bus infrastructure and the device-specific logic.
.Pp
Each driver implements a set of callbacks to handle the lifecycle of devices it supports.
.Sh FIELDS
.Bl -tag -width "match_func"
.It Vt const char *name
Name of the driver (e.g., "ahci", "ne2000").
.It Vt struct bus_type *bus_type
Pointer to the bus type this driver belongs to (e.g., &pci_bus_type).
.It Vt const void *id_table
Pointer to a bus-specific table of device IDs supported by this driver.
.It Vt int (*probe)(struct device *)
Check if a device is supported and hardware exists. Returns 0 on success.
.It Vt int (*attach)(struct device *)
Initialize the device, allocate resources, and register interfaces.
.It Vt int (*detach)(struct device *)
Shutdown the device and release resources.
.It Vt int (*suspend)(struct device *, int)
Suspend device to the specified power state.
.It Vt int (*resume)(struct device *)
Resume device from a suspended state.
.It Vt void (*shutdown)(struct device *)
Called during system shutdown/reboot.
.It Vt int (*reset)(struct device *)
Reset the device hardware execution state.
.It Vt int (*match_func)(struct device *, struct driver *)
Optional custom matching function. Returns non-zero if the driver matches the device.
.It Vt int priority
Driver priority level (higher values indicate higher priority).
.It Vt uint32_t flags
Driver status and capability flags.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bus 9 ,
.Xr device 9
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Vt struct driver
interface first appeared in Substrate.
